A setting is IDENTIFIED when it has at least 20 discriminating rows,
3 intercepts and a band no wider than 0.15. Residual RMS is model
adequacy in log units, not sampling error: if it is far above the timing
repeatability the bands are optimistic and only the ORDER of the alphas survives.

